@@ -12,16 +12,16 @@
 
 INSTALLATION
 
-To install Authen::Krb5::Admin without testing, run the standard
-sequence:
+To build, test and install Authen::Krb5::Admin, run:
 
 	perl Makefile.PL
 	make
+	make test
 	make install
 
-The first step will prompt you for a principal with administrative
-privileges on the KDC for running the test suite.  Re-run this step to
-change which principal to use.
+The default tests load the module and exercise local configuration,
+policy, principal and key objects. They do not require kinit, a Kerberos
+configuration file, credentials or a running KDC.
 
 The build script will attempt to use the krb5-config tool to discover
 the location of your Kerberos installation. This tool is part of the
@@ -50,17 +50,36 @@
 
 TESTING
 
-To run the test suite as part of the install, use
+Signature verification is optional. To request it explicitly, run:
 
-	perl Makefile.PL
+	TEST_SIGNATURE=1 perl t/00-0-signature.t
+
+This requires Module::Signature and the signer's public key. The shipped
+SIGNATURE predates this release, and its checksums do not match the
+release sources. Local patches also invalidate signed checksums. A failed
+signature check does not diagnose a functional or interpreter failure.
+
+To enable the KDC integration tests, configure with:
+
+	PERL_KADM5_TEST_KDC=1 perl Makefile.PL
 	make test
 	make install
 
-This step requires administrative access to the KDC by the principal
-specified in the first step.  It will create a principal, by default
-"perl_test", which should NOT already exist on the KDC.  If you
-already have a principal called perl_test, change Makefile.PL to use a
-different test principal, and start over.
+Makefile.PL will prompt for an administrative principal and two unused
+test principal names. These tests require a configured KDC and kinit in
+KRB5_BINDIR. They create, modify and delete principals and policies, so
+use a test realm. The default test names, "perl_test" and "perl_test_2",
+must not already exist in that realm.
+
+Set PERL_KADM5_PRINCIPAL, PERL_KADM5_TEST_NAME and
+PERL_KADM5_TEST_NAME_2 before running Makefile.PL to supply these values
+without prompts. To use existing credentials instead of running kinit,
+set PERL_KADM5_TEST_CACHE to the credentials cache when configuring.
+The cache must contain a ticket for the kadmin/admin service.
+
+Rerun Makefile.PL without PERL_KADM5_TEST_KDC to return to local tests.
+The KDC option applies to ordinary Perl and XPerl alike. Running the
+local tests does not validate the remote administrative operations.
 
 
 Stephen Quinney <squinney@inf.ed.ac.uk>
